link: Censys, ARTEX: Agentic Asbestos | https://censys.com/blog/artex-agentic-asbestos/
link: Microsoft, ARTEX abuse expands to the financial sector | https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/06/artex-abuse-expands-as-cybercriminals-target-financial-sector/
link: Microsoft, agentic tooling and exposed secrets | https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/05/threat-actors-use-agentic-ai-tooling-to-find-and-abuse-exposed-secrets/
link: MITRE ATT&CK T1552.005 | https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005/
link: MITRE ATT&CK T1574.001 | https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1574/001/
notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

CrowdStrike's report describes the campaign. CyberScoop carries the interview reporting, including the 140 figure. Check Point and Censys counted exposed ARTEX consoles, and Check Point also read the databases of cybercrime operators' instances. Microsoft's two posts cover ARTEX abuse in the financial sector and agentic tooling that finds and abuses exposed secrets. The two MITRE pages define the techniques behind stages 04 and 07.

The background slides name their own sources, from OWASP, AWS, Microsoft Learn and MITRE.

== Related kill chains
layout: links
link: Storm-0940 and ConnectWise | breaches/storm-0940-connectwise.html
link: ARTEX exposed-secrets kill chain | breaches/artex-github-secrets-azure.html
CrowdStrike states this campaign is separate from the ARTEX activity Microsoft attributes to Storm-0940. Microsoft has since linked ARTEX to a separate campaign that turned secrets leaked on GitHub into Azure access.
notes:
Two related kill chains on csoh.org.

CrowdStrike states that this campaign is separate from the ARTEX activity Microsoft attributes to Storm-0940, which has its own kill chain.

Microsoft has since reported a separate campaign it links to ARTEX that turned secrets leaked on GitHub into Azure access. That one is the ARTEX exposed-secrets kill chain, and its guidance on leaked secrets is the one the key rotation defense borrows.

Read them together to see the same framework reported in other campaigns.
